# Building

The implementation uses only Go's standard library (Go 1.21 or newer).
No downloaded modules or project-specific packages are needed.

```sh
./compile.sh
./executable --help
go test ./...
```

The program implements the command-line parser, configuration loader, streaming
line buffer, search filters, terminal renderer, keyboard handling, and selection
state directly. JSON and YAML configuration files are supported. Terminal I/O
uses the controlling terminal, keeping standard output available for selected
records and standard input available for streamed input.

Build products and local exploratory test data are excluded by `.gitignore`.
